<title>GERMANY: Siemens to pay full sick pay - union.</title>
<headline>Siemens to pay full sick pay - union.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siemens AG and its works council have agreed to continue making full wage payments to employees in the event of illness, the trade union IG Metall said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Siemens had originally announced that it would impose 20 percent cuts in sick pay under new rules which took effect on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The move by a group of leading companies, led by auto giant Daimler-Benz AG aroused the fury of trade union leaders, who said guaranteed full sick pay was locked into their labour contracts.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
